ogin":"dugramen","id":54819319,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODE5MzE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54819319?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen","html_url":"https://github.com/dugramen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T23:35:55Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T23:35:55Z","body":"I'll try to rework my fix. I think instead of changing the separation of that vbox, we should probably just add them to a different vbox","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2829072340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2829211862","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104931#issuecomment-2829211862","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104931","id":2829211862,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ooljW","user":{"login":"dugramen","id":54819319,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODE5MzE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54819319?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen","html_url":"https://github.com/dugramen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T02:03:54Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T23:29:45Z","body":"Ok so I did some testing and I'm gonna need some second opinions. \n\nIt turns out, groups are ordered differently than subgroups and `PROPERTY_USAGE_ARRAY` groups. Normal groups are added to a separate vbox at the bottom of the category. That vbox has a separation of 0. \n\nHowever, subgroups and array groups are added to the same vbox as normal properties, so they can be in any order, not just stuck at the bottom. But that also means they can't have their own separation value\n\nSo I can see a few options for this issue:\n1. Revert it back to how it was. Properties and normal groups get the right spacing, but array groups and subgroups don't.\n2. Revert it but move array groups into the same vbox as normal groups. This way only subgroups get the wrong spacing, but array groups are stuck to the bottom\n3. Move all normal groups, subgroups, and array groups to the bottom in their own vbox. This would make all group types have the proper spacing but they all lose their ordering\n4. Remove the dedicated vbox for groups. This would make all groups reorderable, but have that extra spacing. Maybe it looks normal? probably not\n5. Remove the dedicated vbox for groups, and instead do some automatic vbox grouping. When multiple groups are detected next to each other, automatically group them into a new vbox with 0 separation. This would fix any spacing issue, and add the ability for normal groups to be ordered too\n\nI'm interested in exploring 5, if its desired. But if not I can submit 1 or 2 pretty easily\n\nEdit: just submitted a PR for option 5","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2829211862/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]